---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import ContactEmail from '../../components/ContactEmail.astro';
import { LEGAL_ENTITY, LEGAL_ADDRESS, LEGAL_JURISDICTION, PRODUCTS } from '../../config';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Legal
  lang={lang}
  path="/terms"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  title="Terms of Use · Hydravia"
  description="Hydravia terms of use: subscription, free trial, cancellation, limitations and health disclaimer."
>
  <p>
    By downloading and using Hydravia you agree to the terms below. Please read at
    least section 3 (subscription) and section 6 (health disclaimer).
  </p>

  <h2>1. Publisher</h2>
  <p>
    Hydravia is published by <span class="todo">{LEGAL_ENTITY}</span>, at
    <span class="todo">{LEGAL_ADDRESS}</span>. Contact:
    <ContactEmail />.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What the app does</h2>
  <p>
    Hydravia is a hydration aid. It calculates an indicative daily goal from your
    weight, sends reminders at the intervals you choose, and can temporarily block
    apps you have selected until you confirm that you drank.
  </p>
  <p>
    The "I drank it" confirmation is based on your own declaration. The app cannot
    verify that you actually drank, and does not claim to.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Subscription, free trial and cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Hydravia offers a <strong>{PRODUCTS.trialDays}-day</strong> free trial, followed
    by an auto-renewing subscription, billed monthly or yearly. Applicable prices are
    those shown in the app at the time of purchase, in your App Store account's
    currency.
  </p>
  <h3>Automatic renewal</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Payment is charged to your Apple account on confirmation of purchase, or at the
      end of the free trial if you have not cancelled beforehand.
    </li>
    <li>
      The subscription <strong>renews automatically</strong> unless cancelled at least
      <strong>24 hours before the end of the current period</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Renewal is charged within 24 hours prior to the end of the current period, at
      the rate of the selected plan.
    </li>
    <li>
      Any unused portion of a free trial is forfeited when you purchase a
      subscription.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>How to cancel</h3>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time in <strong>iOS Settings → your name →
    Subscriptions</strong>. Subscription management belongs to your Apple account: we
    can neither subscribe nor cancel on your behalf. Cancellation takes effect at the
    end of the period already paid for, during which you keep access.
  </p>
  <h3>Refunds</h3>
  <p>
    Since purchases are processed by Apple, refund requests fall under their policy
    and are made at
    <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. System permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Some features rely on permissions you grant explicitly: notifications (for
    reminders), Screen Time (for the app lock) and location (to adjust the dose to
    the temperature). Each one is optional and revocable in your phone's settings.
    Declining a permission disables the matching feature without preventing you from
    using the rest of the app.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>decompile, reverse-engineer or attempt to extract the app's source code;</li>
    <li>circumvent billing or subscription mechanisms;</li>
    <li>use the app in any way that breaks applicable law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Health disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Hydravia is not a medical device and provides no medical advice.
    </strong>
    The goals and doses it suggests are general estimates derived from your weight,
    the time of day and the temperature. They do not account for your health
    conditions, medication, pregnancy, intense physical activity or any medical
    condition.
  </p>
  <p>
    Water needs vary considerably from person to person, and drinking excessive
    amounts of water can be dangerous. If you are unsure, have a kidney or heart
    condition, or are under treatment, seek advice from a healthcare professional:
    their advice always takes precedence over what the app displays. Listen to your
    thirst.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Availability and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided "as is". We do not warrant that it will be error-free or
    available without interruption. In particular, reminders and the lock depend on
    the operating system, the permissions granted and the state of your device: a
    reminder may fail to fire (airplane mode, low battery, revoked permissions,
    restart).
  </p>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect damages arising
    from the use of, or inability to use, the app. Nothing in these terms limits the
    rights the law grants you as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The app, its name, logo, design and content are protected. Your subscription
    grants a personal, non-exclusive right of use, not a transfer of ownership.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be amended. In the event of a substantial change you will be
    informed in the app or before your subscription renews. Continued use constitutes
    acceptance of the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of
    <span class="todo">{LEGAL_JURISDICTION}</span>. For any question write to
    <ContactEmail />. We always prefer an
    amicable resolution.
  </p>
</Legal>
